-- title:
--   Coefficients of $(q;q)_\infty(X^{11})\cdot(q;q)_\infty$ vanish at residues $3,6,8,9,10$ mod 11
-- statement:
--   Work in $(\mathbb{Z}/11)[[X]]$ with $Q=(q;q)_\infty$ (`qPochInfPS`) and $Q(X^{11})$ its image under $X\mapsto X^{11}$ (`PowerSeries.expand`). For $r\in\{3,6,8,9,10\}$ and every $n\in\mathbb{N}$,
--   $$[X^{11n+r}]\big(Q(X^{11})\,Q\big)=0.$$
--   The reason is that pentagonal numbers are never congruent to these residues mod 11. Chapter 17.
